ing":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"NACCO Industries, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the natural resources business. The company operates through three segments: Utility Coal Mining, Contract Mining, and Minerals and Royalties. The Utility Coal Mining operates surface coal mines under long-term contracts for power plants and a synfuels plant. This segment operates coal mines in North Dakota and Mississippi. The Contract Mining segment provides value-added contract mining and other services for producers of industrial minerals and products; contract mining services for independently owned mines and quarries in Florida, Arkansas, and Nebraska; and dragline services. The Minerals and Royalties segment is involved in the leasing of its royalty and mineral interests to third-party exploration and production companies, and other mining companies, which grants them the rights to explore, develop, mine, produce, market, and sell gas, oil, and coal. The company also provides natural resource restoration and reclamation services that include stream and wetland mitigation solutions. NACCO Industries, Inc. was founded in 1913 and is headquartered in Cleveland, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John C. Butler Jr. | President, CEO & Non-Independent Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 600 people. Revenue per employee of $462K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers, declining at 16%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $4K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["NACCO Industries, Inc. is a micro-cap energy business with a $257M market cap on $277M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and -11% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 21% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $2M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.90\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 33% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 400% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.9987062549294476},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 1136% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"NACCO Industries Inc (NC) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Operating Profit Jumps 37% as New ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nacco-industries-inc-nc-q3-031329093.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793934809.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.214,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NACCO Industries (NC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nacco-industries-nc-q3-2026-220140873.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793916100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Rocky Mount to Host 47th CIAA Volleyball Championship, Spotlighting Eastern NC Sports Tourism","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/rocky-mount-to-host-47th-ciaa-volleyball-championship-spotlighting-eastern-nc-sports-tourism-302929677.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793829600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":