e than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.29 vs 5y 0.60), so read it loosely.","Trading is thin (about $763K a day), below the $1.0M liquidity floor flagged; building a position would move the price.","In past sell-offs it fell 62% in the 2020 crash, 41% in the 2022 bear market and 88% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $6.80 (margin of safety -400%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 48%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $3.69 to $12.20 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Energy peers: P/E 17.3 vs 13.4 and P/FCF 112.3 vs 14.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 89% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 0.9% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The price implies 12.3% annual cash-flow growth, 18pp more than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 10% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.97).","It runs a 21% gross margin and converts 1% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.90x.","ROE of 4% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.5x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.1% of revenue on R&D and 3.0% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.1x net debt to EBITDA ($49.7M of cash against $100.8M of debt), with interest covered 3.8x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.09)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.7% over 3 years, 16.6% over 5 years and -11.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 36%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 113%.","Capex runs 1.9x depreciation (17.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 14, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 33.0%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 37%.","It returns 3.8% a year to shareholders (1.0% in buybacks and 3.1% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.1% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 40 consecutive years, raising it 6.4% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 600 employees, each generates about $462K of revenue, 0.2x the Energy median, and productivity has fallen 16.3% a year.","That works out to $4K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.8M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $14K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":39,"head":"Avoid: priced 400% above its fair value of $6.80.","pros":["Revenue grew 16.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 1.1x","Returns 3.8% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 22, gates 7/24)","Trades 400% above fair value of $6.80","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 17.3x vs sector 13.4x","P/FCF 112.3x vs sector 14.3x"],"flags":["Priced 400% above its fair value of $6.80","The model rates it PASS"],"need":[],"buy_below":5.78,"vc":{"base":6.8,"base_src":"dcf","bear":3.69,"bull":12.2,"alt_median":31.59,"n_alt":3,"gap":-0.7847,"dispersion":0.4834,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (48% dispersion)","DCF is 78% below the other models' median ($31.59)","bull case is 3.3x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":13.3952,"ev_ebitda":6.86,"pfcf":14.299,"pb":1.6885,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0754,"div_yield":0.0371}},"ticker":"NC","date":"2026-11-06"}